And I hated the Celtics too.

00:12:32.238 --> 00:12:33.397
- [Man] We all did, man.

00:12:33.397 --> 00:12:35.683
- DJ, DJ lived in LA.

00:12:35.683 --> 00:12:37.959
So we told DJ before the finals

00:12:37.959 --> 00:12:39.429
that every time we played the Celtics,

00:12:39.429 --> 00:12:41.611
"Hey brother, you the enemy.

00:12:41.611 --> 00:12:42.898
"And so don't talk to me.

00:12:42.898 --> 00:12:43.784
"Can't talk to you."

00:12:43.784 --> 00:12:46.235
(man laughs)

00:12:46.235 --> 00:12:47.881
He was cool, but that's my boy.

00:12:47.881 --> 00:12:50.025
But, mmm-hmm, when you're lined up

00:12:50.025 --> 00:12:51.320
and trying to take something from me,

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:54.421
especially that championship, I hate you.

00:12:54.421 --> 00:12:57.504
(instrumental music)

00:13:00.587 --> 00:13:02.004
- Hold the court.

00:13:03.702 --> 00:13:07.144
Four seconds, three, right at the net.

00:13:07.144 --> 00:13:08.431
He scores!

00:13:08.431 --> 00:13:11.514
(instrumental music)

00:13:15.415 --> 00:13:18.332
I want you to see Magic's reaction.

00:13:19.277 --> 00:13:22.360
He likes it, the fans, he's going on.

00:13:25.687 --> 00:13:29.472
(instrumental music)

00:13:29.472 --> 00:13:32.124
- My father worked two
jobs his whole life.

00:13:32.124 --> 00:13:33.619
- [John] At a GM plant.

00:13:33.619 --> 00:13:35.282
- GM plant for 30 years and then

00:13:35.282 --> 00:13:37.128
he had a trash hauling service.

00:13:37.128 --> 00:13:39.598
So he had his own truck.

00:13:39.598 --> 00:13:43.678
And we would go door to
door, pick up people's trash.

00:13:43.678 --> 00:13:45.851
And it was one situation where

00:13:45.851 --> 00:13:48.518
it was probably seven below zero

00:13:50.672 --> 00:13:53.002
and very cold Saturday morning.

00:13:53.002 --> 00:13:56.835
And my job was to pick
up all the loose trash.

00:13:59.393 --> 00:14:01.476
It was so cold that I got everything

00:14:01.476 --> 00:14:05.384
that I could just grab,
throw it on the truck.

00:14:05.384 --> 00:14:06.430
And I ran to the truck because it

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.106
was just cold, to jump in.

00:14:08.106 --> 00:14:10.422
By the time I got in and the door shut,

00:14:10.422 --> 00:14:13.294
my father opened it back up,

00:14:13.294 --> 00:14:15.596
grabbed me and dragged
me through the snow,

00:14:15.596 --> 00:14:17.528
back to the barrels to say,

00:14:17.528 --> 00:14:20.459
"Son, you did a halfway job.

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:24.126
"And if you do this job
in a halfway manner,

00:14:25.073 --> 00:14:27.258
"you're going to be a
halfway basketball player.

00:14:27.258 --> 00:14:29.613
"You put in 1/2 the time.

00:14:29.613 --> 00:14:32.365
"You only put in 1/2
the time as a student."

00:14:32.365 --> 00:14:35.485
And he said, "You're supposed
to do this job right.

00:14:35.485 --> 00:14:38.283
"So I want you to go get that shovel

00:14:38.283 --> 00:14:40.517
"and I want you to chop the ice,

00:14:40.517 --> 00:14:42.453
"until you can get all the trash

00:14:42.453 --> 00:14:45.680
"that's trapped in the ice
and put it on the truck."

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.253
And that's what happened.

00:14:47.253 --> 00:14:49.581
And so he taught me how
to be a perfectionist

00:14:49.581 --> 00:14:50.932
and do everything the right way.

00:14:50.932 --> 00:14:54.015
(instrumental music)

00:14:56.116 --> 00:14:57.764
- [Announcer] You got to get it.

00:14:57.764 --> 00:14:58.989
You got to put it up.

00:14:58.989 --> 00:15:00.418
You don't get a shot away.

00:15:00.418 --> 00:15:02.538
You'll talk about it
the rest of your life.

00:15:02.538 --> 00:15:05.409
Magic fires for three, he got it!

00:15:05.409 --> 00:15:07.636
That's right, Magic got a three point in!

00:15:07.636 --> 00:15:09.443
And the Lakers won.

00:15:09.443 --> 00:15:12.526
(instrumental music)

00:15:17.865 --> 00:15:20.451
- I got up here, you do not go

00:15:20.451 --> 00:15:22.755
into this Hall of Fame and win

00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:24.672
this honor by yourself.

00:15:28.098 --> 00:15:30.848
Larry, you know, you're just what

00:15:33.973 --> 00:15:36.418
a basketball player should be.

00:15:36.418 --> 00:15:39.418
(audience applauds)

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:48.987
The biggest reason that I'm here

00:15:48.987 --> 00:15:52.138
is because of you making me go

00:15:52.138 --> 00:15:54.221
to that gym every summer.

00:15:55.617 --> 00:15:57.843
Not only staying for four hours.

00:15:57.843 --> 00:16:00.039
But I figure I better stay for six,

00:16:00.039 --> 00:16:01.062
because I knew you were there about

00:16:01.062 --> 00:16:02.350
five or six, yourself.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:05.706
(audience laughs)

00:16:05.706 --> 00:16:08.873
It was tremendous playing against you.

00:16:10.359 --> 00:16:12.442
And I'm just happy.

00:16:12.442 --> 00:16:15.585
And I thank God that I got to know you.

00:16:15.585 --> 00:16:18.069
Not as just Larry Bird,
the basketball player,

00:16:18.069 --> 00:16:19.448
but Larry Bird the man.

00:16:19.448 --> 00:16:21.048
And I appreciate you
coming out here tonight.

00:16:21.048 --> 00:16:22.216
(audience applauds)

00:16:22.216 --> 00:16:25.299
(instrumental music)

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:30.395
- [Announcer] James
Worthy for Magic Johnson,

00:16:30.395 --> 00:16:31.342
in the low-pro.

00:16:31.342 --> 00:16:32.175
He talked about getting Johnson.

00:16:32.175 --> 00:16:33.008
- [Other Announcer] Firey Scott is in

00:16:33.008 --> 00:16:34.808
the ball game now.

00:16:34.808 --> 00:16:36.391
Five seconds to go.

00:16:39.703 --> 00:16:41.407
He scores in two.

00:16:41.407 --> 00:16:44.490
(instrumental music)

00:17:09.888 --> 00:17:11.147
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:17:11.147 --> 00:17:13.321
I made this video
because Zano asked me to.

00:17:13.321 --> 00:17:14.687
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:17:14.687 --> 00:17:16.804
you want me to profile next, then leave

00:17:16.804 --> 00:17:17.918
it in the comments below.

00:17:17.918 --> 00:17:18.925
And I'll see what I can do.

00:17:18.925 --> 00:17:19.898
I'd also love to know which of

00:17:19.898 --> 00:17:21.393
Magic Johnson's Top 10 Rules had

00:17:21.393 --> 00:17:23.638
the biggest impact on you and why.

00:17:23.638 --> 00:17:24.656
What change you're going to make

00:17:24.656 --> 00:17:25.698
in your business as a result of

00:17:25.698 --> 00:17:27.177
watching this video.

00:17:27.177 --> 00:17:28.422
Leave it in the comments.

00:17:28.422 --> 00:17:29.972
And I will join in the discussion.

00:17:29.972 --> 00:17:31.561
Thank you so much for watching.

00:17:31.561 --> 00:17:35.061
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

00:17:40.477 --> 00:17:43.919
- It's not enough for us
just to deliver anymore.

00:17:43.919 --> 00:17:45.752
We got to over deliver.

00:17:47.238 --> 00:17:48.590
If you want to keep all the billions

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.423
of customers you have,

00:17:51.684 --> 00:17:53.061
and hundreds, and hundreds, of million

00:17:53.061 --> 00:17:57.246
customers you have, you have
to over deliver to them.

00:17:57.246 --> 00:18:00.246
Like the G Phone, it over delivered.

00:18:01.615 --> 00:18:04.592
So you got to over deliver.

00:18:04.592 --> 00:18:08.592
And so we've been able
to do that with our fund.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:14.237
They turned me down a couple
times, CalSTRS, CalPERS.

00:18:14.237 --> 00:18:16.538
And they wanted me to really come back

00:18:16.538 --> 00:18:21.025
and understand that if
they gave me this money,

00:18:21.025 --> 00:18:22.817
and the reason they're giving it to me.

00:18:22.817 --> 00:18:24.756
First they turned me
down for the reasons of,

00:18:24.756 --> 00:18:26.820
I didn't have the track record

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:28.605
that they thought I should have.

00:18:28.605 --> 00:18:31.620
And then they said, "If this business

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:33.763
"strategy is so great, why isn't

00:18:33.763 --> 00:18:36.513
"somebody else doing it already?"

00:18:37.702 --> 00:18:39.925
And I couldn't answer that.

00:18:39.925 --> 00:18:41.412
So they said, "What we're going to do,

00:18:41.412 --> 00:18:44.912
"we're going to give
you 50 million dollars."

00:18:46.013 --> 00:18:48.015
Because I was there for 150 million.

00:18:48.015 --> 00:18:50.928
But they said, "We'll give you 50."

00:18:50.928 --> 00:18:51.761
I said, "I'm African American.

00:18:51.761 --> 00:18:52.695
"I'll take that."

00:18:52.695 --> 00:18:55.178
(audience laughs)

00:18:55.178 --> 00:18:57.761
Five dollars I would have took.

00:19:00.859 --> 00:19:03.942
And if you deliver upon your promise,

00:19:05.151 --> 00:19:08.556
you can come back and
access the other 100.

00:19:08.556 --> 00:19:12.731
So I bought a shopping
center for 22 million.

00:19:12.731 --> 00:19:16.995
It was only about 40% or
50% occupied at that time.

00:19:16.995 --> 00:19:19.761
We brought it up to 100% occupied.

00:19:19.761 --> 00:19:24.353
We sold that same shopping
center for 48 million dollars.

00:19:24.353 --> 00:19:26.406
So did I over deliver?

00:19:26.406 --> 00:19:29.447
Yes, that's a lot of money they got.

00:19:29.447 --> 00:19:32.216
And a lot of return on their investment.

00:19:32.216 --> 00:19:33.790
So I was able to go from there.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:36.325
It took, to access the 100 million.

00:19:36.325 --> 00:19:38.989
But also raise my first real estate fund,

00:19:38.989 --> 00:19:42.381
which took us almost three years

00:19:42.381 --> 00:19:43.665
to raise 300 million dollars.

00:19:43.665 --> 00:19:47.088
We returned our partners
30% on their money.

00:19:47.088 --> 00:19:48.871
They were very happy.

00:19:48.871 --> 00:19:50.625
So how long you think it took me

00:19:50.625 --> 00:19:52.262
to raise 600 million?

00:19:52.262 --> 00:19:55.044
After we returned them 30% on their money?

00:19:55.044 --> 00:19:57.346
Almost less than a year.

00:19:57.346 --> 00:19:59.621
We raised 600 million.

00:19:59.621 --> 00:20:02.817
We just returned them about 18% to 20%

00:20:02.817 --> 00:20:05.108
on their money, very happy.

00:20:05.108 --> 00:20:06.564
And then before the market crashed,

00:20:06.564 --> 00:20:08.941
knock on wood, we just raised a billion

00:20:08.941 --> 00:20:10.620
dollars in cash.

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:12.892
And we're ready to go out and invest.

00:20:12.892 --> 00:20:14.337
It still blows you away.

00:20:14.337 --> 00:20:17.170
You know, that somebody would want

00:20:18.118 --> 00:20:21.835
to have your jersey on, with your name.

00:20:21.835 --> 00:20:24.411
Want to go in your business.

00:20:24.411 --> 00:20:27.491
And frequent that business.

00:20:27.491 --> 00:20:31.408
And want to take their
family to your business.

00:20:33.577 --> 00:20:36.244
It's been a humbling experience.

00:20:38.244 --> 00:20:41.297
Sometime early on and I still do it now,

00:20:41.297 --> 00:20:45.464
I just go park the car and
watch people go in and out.

00:20:46.836 --> 00:20:50.586
And know that you have
affected the community

00:20:51.583 --> 00:20:53.500
in such a positive way.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.133
And then sometimes I cry.

00:20:57.133 --> 00:20:58.419
I guess God put me on this Earth

00:20:58.419 --> 00:21:02.002
to do some special
things for other people.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:04.438
It's not about me, it's about

00:21:04.438 --> 00:21:07.438
the community, and making it better.

00:21:11.656 --> 00:21:13.309
And I'm glad I've done that.

